steps.human:
getFlows walks *.flow.json and parses each readable record; it does not read product-truth index.json. It also appends the separate artifact-knowledge-graph document as an architecture view. Parsing and AC resolution below are internal phases of the same call, not separate JSON endpoints. The per-repository cache means these are load-time values, not a polling promise. [Producer](leafcutter-web/lib/data/flows.ts) and [normalized types](leafcutter-web/lib/data/types.ts).

Contract fields and examples (generated)
Consumes:
  raw_flow/id: string (required)
  raw_flow/component: string (required)
  raw_flow/kind: string (required)
  raw_flow/source: string (required)
  raw_flow/steps/*/id: string (required)
  raw_flow/steps/*/implements: array (optional)
  raw_flow/steps/*/impl_status: string (optional)
  Schema: [raw_flow](docs/product-truth/schemas/flow.schema.json)
Produces:
  SOURCE-REVIEWED DOCUMENTATION: Source-reviewed documentation of leafcutter-web/lib/data/types.ts, flow-contracts.ts and flows.ts; no runtime registration or automatic TypeScript/schema parity check.
  atlas_flow/id: string (required)
  atlas_flow/component: string (required)
  atlas_flow/kind: string (required)
  atlas_flow/source: string (required)
  atlas_flow/steps/*/id: string (required)
  atlas_flow/steps/*/implements: array (required)
  atlas_flow/steps/*/implStatus: string (required)
  atlas_flow/filePath: string (required)
  atlas_flow/contractDefinitions: object (optional)
  atlas_flow/steps/*/ioContracts: object (optional)
  atlas_flow/branches/*/ioContracts: object (optional)
  Schema: [atlas_flow](docs/product-truth/schemas/atlas-normalized-flow.schema.json)

Input: selected stored snake_case fields — raw_flow; illustrative; selected fields only; full required/defaulted fields in linked contract:
