  "id": "leafcutter/flow-render-pipeline",
  "component": "ux-prototyping",
  "kind": "data",
  "source": "real",
  "steps": [
    {
      "id": "resolve",
      "implements": [
        "UXP-411"
      ],
      "impl_status": "done"
    }
  ]
}

Output: reconstructed normalized camelCase fields; selected fields only — atlas_flow; reconstructed; selected fields only; full required/defaulted fields in linked contract:
{
  "id": "leafcutter/flow-render-pipeline",
  "component": "ux-prototyping",
  "name": "How a flow renders in the Atlas",
  "kind": "data",
  "source": "real",
  "level": "pipeline",
  "realization": "built",
  "mockDataRef": null,
  "filePath": "docs/product-truth/flows/leafcutter/flow-render-pipeline.flow.json",
  "steps": [
    {
      "id": "resolve",
      "label": "Resolve live AC status",
      "implements": [
        "UXP-411"
      ],
      "implStatus": "done",
      "fallbackStatus": "done",
      "acs": [
        {
          "id": "UXP-411",
          "workStatus": "done",
          "resolved": true
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

Output: optional structured metadata, one selected input binding only — atlas_flow; reconstructed; selected fields only; full required/defaulted fields in linked contract:
{
  "contractDefinitions": {
    "raw_flow": {
      "schema": "docs/product-truth/schemas/flow.schema.json"
    }
  },
  "steps": [
    {
      "id": "resolve",
      "ioContracts": {
        "consumes": [
          {
            "contract": "raw_flow",
            "fields": [
              {
                "path": "/steps/*/id",
                "types": [
                  "string"
                ],
                "required": true
              },
              {
                "path": "/steps/*/implements",
                "types": [
                  "array"
                ],
                "required": false
              },
              {
                "path": "/steps/*/impl_status",
                "types": [
                  "string"
                ],
                "required": false
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}

FlowsPage assembles flows, mocks keyed by flow ID, and screenTitles, and passes those serializable props to FlowsView. The client builds graph nodes/edges and renders React/DOM; the visual result is not a new service-response DTO. The example is a selected-field projection of these props, not a complete Flow record. [Server handoff](leafcutter-web/app/flows/page.tsx), [consumer](leafcutter-web/components/flows/flows-view.tsx), [graph construction](leafcutter-web/lib/data/graph.ts). Structured ioContracts and contractDefinitions travel with each flow. The drawer renders contract groups, field tables and separate JSON examples once, hiding generated compatibility copies only when the metadata passes its display guard.

